# Sound the Trumpets recruits only if the countered spell's mana value was 2
# or less (SVar:X:SpellTargeted$CardManaCostLKI, AbilityUtils.java:637-640,
# :2231-2243). Java reads the target SpellAbility's host, the Card object that
# was on the stack: Zone.remove leaves its zone Stack (Zone.java:162-167), so
# getCMC still adds the X paid (Card.java:7350-7353). Endless One cast with
# X=3 had mana value 3, so ai does not recruit and keeps its Plains in the
# library; its printed mana value 0 would have recruited.
startturn human
advance 3
tapformana human 2 G
tapformana human 3 G
tapformana human 4 G
queue payx 3
queue paygeneric G
queue paygeneric G
queue paygeneric G
castspell human 1
tapformana ai 30 U
tapformana ai 31 U
tapformana ai 32 U
queue paygeneric U
queue targets 1
castspell ai 33
resolvestack
